# WezTerm agent rules

Use this file when you change files in `.config/wezterm/`.

Keep this file short. Add only decisions and learnings that are hard to infer from code.

## WezTerm lessons

- Always validate WezTerm pane and split changes before you finish. For split work, run repeated `Left`, `Right`, `Up`, and `Down` stress checks.
- Use `wezterm.org` as the canonical docs site. Treat `wezfurlong.org/wezterm` as legacy until you verify the page is current.
- When split behavior differs by direction, reason from pane geometry and split-tree insertion order. If one direction pair passes and the opposite pair fails, inspect the active band before you change code.
- Keep rebalance work synchronous unless you can prove that retries are needed. Timer-heavy loops have crashed WezTerm here.

